{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-96814" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨5a-2b,\\,c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨c,a⟩=-1+\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨b,c⟩=3-2\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-96814" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨5a-2b,\\,c⟩ & =⟨5a,c⟩-⟨2b,c⟩ \\\\  & =5⟨a,c⟩-2⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5⟨a,c⟩-2⟨b,c⟩ & =5\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}-2⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨c,a⟩$ and $⟨b,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}-2⟨b,c⟩ & =5(\\overset{―}{-1+\\text{i}})-2(3-2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =5(-1-\\text{i})-2(3-2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =-5-5\\text{i}-6+4\\text{i} \\\\  & =-11-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-96814" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ecad5e45f6fee84e172d610a2dd5d10fb72451be8617d401fa0f98bac444cae"} {"question" "q-96814" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-96814" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1-2\\text{i}"] ["math" "-11+9\\text{i}"] ["math" "-11-\\text{i}"] ["math" "-7+9\\text{i}"] ["math" "-7-\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-96814" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-11-\\text{i}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨\\text{i}a,\\,b+c⟩$ if \n\n  $⟨a,b⟩=3-2\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨c,a⟩=2+\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\text{i}a,\\,b+c⟩ & =⟨\\text{i}a,b⟩+⟨\\text{i}a,c⟩ \\\\  & =\\text{i}⟨a,b⟩+\\text{i}⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}⟨a,b⟩+\\text{i}⟨a,c⟩ & =\\text{i}⟨a,b⟩+\\text{i}\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨a,b⟩$ and $⟨c,a⟩:$    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}⟨a,b⟩+\\text{i}\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩} & =\\text{i}(3-2\\text{i})+\\text{i}\\overset{―}{(2+\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\text{i}(3-2\\text{i})+\\text{i}(2-\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2+3\\text{i}+1+2\\text{i} \\\\  & =3+5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ecad5e45f6fee84e172d610a2dd5d10fb72451be8617d401fa0f98bac444cae"} {"question" "q-97200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\text{i}"] ["math" "2-3\\text{i}"] ["math" "3+5\\text{i}"] ["math" "5-2\\text{i}"] ["math" "5\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3+5\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,b⟩=⟨b,a⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨ia,ia⟩=⟨a,a⟩$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the linearity in the first argument  and the antilinearity in the second argument we have\n\n$$\n⟨ia,ia⟩=(i\\cdot \\overset{¯}{i})⟨a,a⟩=-{i}^{2}⟨a,a⟩=⟨a,a⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number, in general.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ecad5e45f6fee84e172d610a2dd5d10fb72451be8617d401fa0f98bac444cae"} {"question" "q-97229" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97229" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97229" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,-ia⟩=-i⟨a,a⟩$ for any nonzero vector  $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false.  By the antilinearity of $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$  in the second argument we have \n\n$$\n⟨a,-ia⟩=\\overset{―}{(-i)}⟨a,a⟩=i⟨a,a⟩\\ne -i⟨a,a⟩\n$$\n\n \nfor any nonzero vector  $a\\in {C}^{n}.$\n\n- Statement II  is true. Indeed, the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number in general.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ecad5e45f6fee84e172d610a2dd5d10fb72451be8617d401fa0f98bac444cae"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-97306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-141162" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨a,\\,2b+(3-2\\text{i})c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨b,a⟩=1-\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,c⟩=3\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-141162" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is antilinear in the second argument:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,\\,2b+(3-2\\text{i})c⟩ & =⟨a,2b⟩+⟨a,(3-2\\text{i})c⟩ \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{2}⟨a,b⟩+(\\overset{―}{3-2\\text{i}})⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨a,b⟩+(3+2\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2⟨a,b⟩+(3+2\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩ & =2\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+(3+2\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨b,a⟩$ and $⟨a,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+(3+2\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩ & =2\\cdot \\overset{―}{1-\\text{i}}+(3+2\\text{i})\\cdot (3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (1+\\text{i})-6+9\\text{i} \\\\  & =-4+11\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-141162" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ecad5e45f6fee84e172d610a2dd5d10fb72451be8617d401fa0f98bac444cae"} {"question" "q-141162" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-141162" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4+11\\text{i}"] ["math" "-4+8\\text{i}"] ["math" "11+8\\text{i}"] ["math" "7+6\\text{i}"] ["math" "8-4\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056035/state.json" "file_sha256" "120803c1848cbaf22b03037d7996452f8cecc795e2766d5514255c386b203b91"} {"question" "q-141162" "fie